    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299">

                <pb facs="0363" n="1197" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/607</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schmedeman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-26T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 26, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>396. Legation 871, July 8, 7 p.m. Any agreements of the character referred to by
                    you should, so far as relates to the United States, be between the trade
                    association in question and the War Trade Board of the United States and signed
                    on behalf of the War Trade Board by the representative of the War Trade Board at
                    Christiania. Before agreements are actually signed, however, explicit authority
                    should be awaited. When agreements are in final form please advise as to what,
                    if any, modifications have been made in the drafts submitted to War Trade Board
                    by Sheldon in his despatch of June 7, 1918.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d299-f1"/>
                    Repeat to Sheldon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
